# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# You usually do not need to do this by hand -- scripts/dev_up.sh generates
# credentials on first run and writes them to a gitignored .env at the
# repository root, where Docker Compose also reads them, so the LiveKit server
# and the gateway cannot drift apart.
#
# Every setting here has a VMA_ prefix and a default in
# src/media_gateway/config.py. Only the LiveKit credentials are mandatory, and
# only when VMA_MEDIA_SOURCE=livekit.

# --- Required for the LiveKit media source ---------------------------------
# Generate your own. The service refuses LiveKit's well-known devkey/secret and
# the spike's published pair, and requires at least 32 characters, so a copied
# credential fails at startup rather than shipping.
#
#   VMA_LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 24)
# These placeholders are deliberately too short to pass validation, so copying
# this file without editing it fails at startup instead of looking like it
# worked.
VMA_LIVEKIT_API_KEY=replace-me
VMA_LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=replace-me

# --- Commonly changed in dev -----------------------------------------------
# scripted needs no LiveKit at all and is what CI runs.
VMA_MEDIA_SOURCE=livekit

# strict rejects anything that is not the expected size, matching the spike.
# first_frame_wins latches the first accepted size per epoch -- use it with a
# real webcam, which is probably 1280x720 rather than 320x180.
VMA_DIMENSION_GUARD_MODE=first_frame_wins

# dev | ci | deploy. deploy additionally requires VMA_INTERNAL_API_TOKEN and
# VMA_DEVICE_ID_ALLOWLIST, and serves no OpenAPI schema or /dev routes.
VMA_ENVIRONMENT=dev

# --- Authorization ---------------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset in dev, and the console leaves its own unset to match. Setting
# it here alone makes Publish fail with 401: the console only sends a token if
# it was built with VITE_VMA_INTERNAL_API_TOKEN, so the two have to be set
# together or not at all.
# VMA_INTERNAL_API_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated, NOT JSON. A JSON value is refused rather than misread.
# VMA_DEVICE_ID_ALLOWLIST=glasses-01,glasses-02

# Pairing codes default to 120 seconds and are consumed once. Device credentials
# default to seven days and rotate when VMA_INTERNAL_API_TOKEN rotates.
# VMA_PAIRING_CODE_TTL_S=120
# VMA_DEVICE_CREDENTIAL_TTL_S=604800

# --- Networking ------------------------------------------------------------
# How this process reaches LiveKit.
# VMA_LIVEKIT_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:7880

# How a device reaches LiveKit. Differs from the above once the gateway and the
# server are separate containers: `livekit` resolves on the internal Compose
# network and nowhere else. Defaults to VMA_LIVEKIT_URL.
# VMA_LIVEKIT_PUBLIC_URL=

# --- Privacy ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Only 0 is accepted. The knob exists so the privacy checklist has something
# concrete to point at; this service retains no raw media.
VMA_RAW_BUFFER_SECONDS=0
